    <ix:continuation id="ct-nonNumeric-0ebc1d21-bc02-46a1-872a-8c8af83763dd-continuation-7" continuedAt="ct-nonNumeric-0ebc1d21-bc02-46a1-872a-8c8af83763dd-continuation-8"><div><p dir="ltr" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 10pt;line-height: 108%;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap; font-size: 10pt;font-style: normal;font-weight: normal;margin: 0;padding: 0;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;line-height: 108%;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap; font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;font-style: normal;font-weight: bold;margin: 0;padding: 0;">Note 7 - Loans Receivable and Allowance for Credit Losses (Continued)</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;line-height: 108%;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap; font-size: 8pt;font-style: normal;font-weight: normal;margin: 0;padding: 0;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;line-height: 108%;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap; font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;font-style: normal;font-weight: normal;margin: 0;padding: 0;">The tables below set forth the amounts and types of non-accrual loans in the Bank&#8217;s loan portfolio at June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025. Loans are placed on non-accrual status when they become more than 90 days delinquent, or earlier if the collection of principal and/or interest become doubtful. </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;line-height: 108%;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap; font-size: 8pt;font-style: normal;font-weight: normal;margin: 0;padding: 0;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;line-height: 108%;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"><ix:nonNumeric name="us-gaap:ScheduleOfFinancingReceivablesNonAccrualStatusTableTextBlock" id="ct-nonNumeric-52b249d0-7f01-4d86-93e5-843e8d4eef99" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2026_To_6_30_2026" escape="true" continuedAt="ct-nonNumeric-52b249d0-7f01-4d86-93e5-843e8d4eef99-continuation-0"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap; font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;font-style: normal;font-weight: normal;margin: 0;padding: 0;">As of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025, non-accrual loans differed from total loans past due 90 days or more because loans that were previously more than 90 days past due are maintained on non-accrual status for a minimum of six months or until the borrower has demonstrated their ability to satisfy the terms of the loan.  </span></ix:nonNumeric></p><ix:continuation id="ct-nonNumeric-52b249d0-7f01-4d86-93e5-843e8d4eef99-continuation-0"><p dir="ltr" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 8pt;line-height: 108%;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap; font-size: 8pt;font-style: normal;font-weight: normal;margin: 0;padding: 0;"> </span></p><p dir="ltr" style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', 'serif';font-size: 1pt;line-height: 108%;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: 0;margin-top: 0;text-align: justify;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap; font-size: 1pt;font-style: normal;font-weight: normal;margin: 0;padding: 0;"> </span></p><div style="text-align:left"><table dir="ltr" style="border: none;border-collapse: collapse;margin-bottom: .001pt;margin-left: 0;margin-right: auto;width: 100%;"><tr s